<title>FRANCE: Elf and Total shares rise in wake of BP results.</title>
<headline>Elf and Total shares rise in wake of BP results.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Elf Aquitaine and Total rose strongly on Wednesday in the wake of better than expected British Petroleum results, dealers said.</p>
<p>The rise of the dollar against the mark was also a supporting factor, they added.</p>
<p>At 1231 GMT, Total was up 6.29 percent at 642 francs and Elf up 4.31 percent at 702 while the CAC-40 blue-chip index was up 1.89 percent at 3040.60 points.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
